# ramon_accept SYSMON limits
#
# Copy to /etc/ramon/accept_limits.conf (read by default) or pass with
# --limits FILE. One reading per line: name, minimum, maximum.
#   temp_ps, temp_pl       temperatures in degrees C (default -40 .. 125)
#   ps.<rail>, pl.<rail>   voltages in V; the rail names are the ones the
#                          sysmon step prints
# A rail without a line is printed but not checked.
#
# The voltage lines below are commented out on purpose: they are the
# recommended operating ranges of Zynq UltraScale+ RFSoC devices with 0.85 V
# cores, taken as a starting point. Check each against the data sheet of the
# fitted part (speed grade: some run VCCINT at 0.72 V) and against the board
# schematic before enabling it. Leave some margin for the SYSMON's own
# measurement error.

temp_ps   -40  100
temp_pl   -40  100

# PS rails, as measured by the PS SYSMON
#ps.vcc_psintlp   0.808  0.892
#ps.vcc_psintfp   0.808  0.892
#ps.vcc_psaux     1.710  1.890
#ps.vcco_psddr    1.140  1.260     # DDR4 at 1.2 V
#ps.ps_mgtravcc   0.825  0.876
#ps.ps_mgtravtt   1.746  1.854

# PL rails, as measured by the PL SYSMON
#pl.vccint        0.825  0.876
#pl.vccaux        1.746  1.854
#pl.vccbram       0.825  0.876
#pl.vcc_psintlp   0.808  0.892
#pl.vcc_psintfp   0.808  0.892
#pl.vcc_psaux     1.710  1.890
